    "body": "Qualification-only PR for the Scope 6E V2 portable package input corrective.\n\nExact candidate:\n\n<PUT NEW COMMIT SHA HERE>\n\nStarting qualified baseline:\n\nd22b9c89f79446fbfea2480e98e807f8da4dfbf4\n\nCorrective:\n\n- portable release membership is derived from the pinned committed Git tree\n- committed bytes come from raw Git blobs rather than checkout bytes\n- arbitrary untracked files cannot enter qualified release archives\n- LF/CRLF checkout representation cannot change qualified archive bytes\n- binary committed bytes remain exact\n- Git-free operation requires explicit snapshot mode\n- independent verifier remains commit-bound for qualified verification\n\nReal witness closure already observed before commit:\n\n- clean/populated archives byte-identical\n- SHA256 c7b9d7a14c88b9c2330ee601e92eeb60434ad6c3f9438f1b5509763c0eb7a1b2\n- 939 entries\n- 883 files\n- 56 directories\n- all 22 untracked Scope 6D scripts excluded\n- prior local-install/path-alias fixes remain intact\n\nEngineering gates:\n\n- 287/287 test files PASS\n- lint PASS\n- build PASS\n- build:github PASS\n- production audit: 0 vulnerabilities\n- no historical assertions weakened\n\nImportant:\n\nThese results were obtained on the uncommitted corrective bytes.\nThe new committed SHA still requires exact-SHA qualification.\n\nDo not merge yet.\n\nPurpose:\n\n- bind CPU/cross-platform CI to the exact corrective candidate\n- rerun package reproducibility from committed bytes\n- perform final exact-SHA corrective closure\n- resume Scope 6E integrated qualification only after this corrective is separately qualified",
